  message: <<EOM
The core needs PC-98 BIOS files in a folder named "np2kai" inside the
frontend's system directory: bios.rom, itf.rom, sound.rom and font.bmp
(or FONT.ROM).

Leave out d8000.rom (the real IDE BIOS). With it, floppy images wait
several minutes on a black screen before booting. Hard disk images
still boot without it.

PC-98 games ran on very different machines, and some need more memory
or a faster CPU than the defaults. Change those settings per game
(in RetroArch: Manage Core Options, Save Game Options), so one game's
settings don't break another.

The core writes to the disk images it runs, so keep a copy of the
originals.

The core doesn't support .m3u playlists. To load several images (e.g.
two floppy disks, or a boot floppy and a CD), list them in a .cmd file,
using paths without spaces, and load that file as content:

  np2kai /path/to/disk1.hdm /path/to/disk2.hdm
EOM
}
